  "published": "2026-10-28T06:07:37.157Z",
  "releaseNotes": "5.0.0:\nBreaking changes: the generated XML changed, existing documents can still be read.\n- decimals keep their precision and are always written culture-invariant\n- FVALUE_TYPE written in lower case, QuantityCodes.Unknown no longer written\n- no type attribute on ORDERRESPONSE, schema namespaces for TAX_NUMBER, PRICE_UNIT, PRICE_UNIT_FACTOR\n- GenerationDate written as set, ORDER_PARTIES_REFERENCE derived from parties if not set\n- AUTHENTIFICATION written with LOGIN/PASSWORD, element order of FEATURE and ORDERRESPONSE_INFO corrected\nNew:\n- targets netstandard2.0, net8.0 and net10.0\n- LoadAsync/SaveAsync with CancellationToken for Order and OrderResponse\n- OrderResponse: DeliveryDate, OrderPartiesReference, Currency, Remarks\n- Contact.AuthentificationPassword\n- reading of PARTIAL_SHIPMENT_ALLOWED, CUSTOMER_ORDER_REFERENCE, TOTAL_AMOUNT, BUYER_PID, CONTACT_ROLE, FORDER, FTEMPLATE\nBugfixes:\n- crashes when saving default Party/Contact objects, partial OrderPartiesReference, phone numbers without type\n- file handles left open by OrderResponse.Load(file)\n\n4.0.2:\nadditional documentation\n\n4.0.1:\ncorrected element order\nimproved code safety. some additional null checks\n\n4.0.0:\nSome breaking changes inside.\nBugfixes.\nDocumentation added.\n\n3.0.0:\nError correction around email addresses in parties and contacts.\n\n2.2.0:\nadding Feature and more fields\n\n2.1.0:\nrepacked.\n\n2.0.0: full support for order response message\n1.3.0: correction of net standard configuration in nuget package\n1.2.0: converted into .net standard 2.0, made dates optional values\n1.1.0: fixed bug in order creation, added support for all countries, moved to .net 4.6.2\n1.0.0: Initial",
